DEBUG ONLY -- NOT PART OF ANY BUILD.

Markers inside tcc_set_output_type, which is where the driver dies:

    T1  entered, about to set output_type
    T2  about to add the system include path
    T3  system include path added
    T4  about to call tccelf_new
    T5  tccelf_new returned
    T6  about to add the library path
    T7  library path added

The driver-level markers narrowed it to this function; these narrow it to a
statement. Same reason as before -- four guesses at what tcc_new was doing
were all wrong, and reading emitted code only helps once there is a specific
statement to read.

